WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.750
A foreign judgment isn't automatically enforceable in the UAE.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:06.630
First, petition the Execution Judge.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:09.230
A decision is due within five working days.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:11.890
The judge checks the foreign court had jurisdiction,

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:14.050
and that the parties were properly summoned and represented,

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:17.190
that the judgment was lawfully issued and authenticated,

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:19.130
and has become final (res judicata),

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:22.130
and doesn't conflict with an earlier UAE ruling,

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:23.970
or with public order and morals.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:27.230
The same rules cover foreign arbitral awards,

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:30.210
notarised deeds and certified settlements.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.370
The judge's order can be appealed.

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:35.630
Judgment abroad, assets in the UAE?

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:38.300
Enforcement follows a defined legal path.
